# pypdf's DictionaryObject.read_from_stream parses dictionary key/value
# pairs in an unbounded `while True` loop over the PDF byte stream, and
# its recovery policy converts every parsing error into warn-and-continue
# in non-strict mode: the broad `except Exception` handler logs, returns
# partial data, and the key-parse `except PdfReadError` handler logs and
# continues. Two guards raise on attacker-driven non-progress -- the
# reader's self-reference cycle guard over _known_objects, and
# RecursionError on deeply nested objects -- and in non-strict mode the
# broad handler absorbs both: the failing parse consumed nothing, so the
# retry re-reads the same bytes, raises the same error, and the loop
# never reaches an exit (CWE-835/CWE-400; GHSA-87mj-5ggw-8qc3, shipped
# in 6.9.2). The fix has two halves: the reader's cycle guard raises
# LimitReachedError instead of PdfReadError, and the dictionary parser
# adds `except (RecursionError, LimitReachedError): raise
# PdfReadError(...)` ahead of the broad handler, so those two classes
# always propagate. The ordinary-malformed-input PdfReadError handler
# stays in both revisions -- lenient recovery for correctable input is
# the library's non-strict design, not the defect. Pool commit 02b1345
# is the fix (PR #3693); the release commit da867f49 names it in its
# changelog, and the advisory's own reference (COMMIT_NONE, no commit
# cited) resolves to it. No pool correction.
#
# Held ATTENTION, lenient-recovery family (the unbounded-parse group
# with 1517, 1554, 1572, 1586 and 1612), rechecked at the span tip.
# Fresh 3 x --cache off scans of the pypdf package at 02b1345^ and
# 02b1345 report 65 findings at both revisions with identical rule
# tallies (54 VYQL-AUTH-099, 8 VYQL-PATH-001, 8 VYQL-CRY-001, 4
# VYQL-DOS-001, 4 VYQL-CRY-002, 3 VYQL-INJ-015, 1 VYQL-INJ-003, 1
# VYQL-DOS-042, 1 VYQL-DESER-002); a whole-checkout scan passes the
# 180s bound, and the package subtree holds both changed files. The
# rows reaching into read_from_stream are two AUTH-099 mass-assignment
# findings -- source the stream parameter, sink retval.update(data)
# inside the recovery handler -- present at both revisions (the sink
# shifts two lines); they judge bulk assignment, not the loop. `vyql
# match` on the file reports 143 ExternalEntryInput parameter labels
# and a MassAssignmentSink; no loop, exception, raise or restart label
# exists, and the Python frontend emits no such fact: the generic
# function-context tokens are assign:/assign_item:/assign_call:/
# call_path:/call:/selector:/identifier:/subscript:/literal:, and the
# control-facts machinery carries session provenance and guard
# correlation only.
#
# The vocabulary verdict holds against the current knowledge base.
# VYQL-DOS-029's concept is bound in C only. VYQL-DOS-050
# (LoopRestartWithoutProgress) is the CWE-835 progress rule shipped
# after the family entries were written, and its binding is
# JavaScript-only; its frontend fact is not emitted for a condition
# that reads no variable (`while (true)`, javascript.go jsLoopRestart),
# and its judgement analyses restart structure, which this fix does
# not change: the `except PdfReadError` continue is present at both
# revisions, and the restart the CVE turns on is covered evidence in
# the fact's own sense anyway -- the loop head re-assigns the break
# guard's variable (`tok = read_non_whitespace(stream)`) on every path
# to every restart, so a ported fact sees progress and stays silent at
# both revisions. What the fact cannot model is that the re-read yields
# the same bytes because the failing parse consumed nothing, which is
# error-class semantics: the discriminating question is which error
# classes a recovery handler must not absorb, and the only textual
# difference between the revisions is the added except clause naming
# them, the fixing commit's own layout. A compact-body-text route
# (`exceptException` plus `continue`) is silenceable by a comment and
# fires on every broad-except retry loop in ordinary code; a binding
# on pypdf's logger_warning detects this library rather than weakness.
# No standalone ENGINE-GAPS.md entry: no taint path is involved and no
# single construct is mishandled. No definition change shipped. This
# spec pins both revisions of both halves of the fix, rejecting
# VYQL-DOS-029 and VYQL-DOS-050: when lenient-recovery vocabulary
# lands, the swallowed-limit form must flip to expect on whichever
# fires.

test "rank1627: the lenient dictionary parser absorbs the limit errors"
  lang python
  file pypdf/generic/_data_structures.py
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  reject VYQL-DOS-050
  code
  ```
  class DictionaryObject(dict):
      @staticmethod
      def read_from_stream(stream, pdf, forced_encoding=None):
          tmp = stream.read(2)
          if tmp != b"<<":
              raise PdfReadError(STREAM_TRUNCATED_PREMATURELY)
          data = {}
          while True:
              tok = read_non_whitespace(stream)
              if tok == b"\x00":
                  continue
              if tok == b"%":
                  stream.seek(-1, 1)
                  skip_over_comment(stream)
                  continue
              if not tok:
                  raise PdfStreamError(STREAM_TRUNCATED_PREMATURELY)
              if tok == b">":
                  stream.read(1)
                  break
              stream.seek(-1, 1)
              try:
                  try:
                      key = read_object(stream, pdf)
                      if isinstance(key, NullObject):
                          break
                      if not isinstance(key, NameObject):
                          raise PdfReadError(
                              f"Expecting a NameObject for key but found {key!r}"
                          )
                  except PdfReadError as exc:
                      if pdf is not None and pdf.strict:
                          raise
                      logger_warning(exc.__repr__(), __name__)
                      continue
                  tok = read_non_whitespace(stream)
                  stream.seek(-1, 1)
                  value = read_object(stream, pdf, forced_encoding)
              except Exception as exc:
                  if pdf is not None and pdf.strict:
                      raise PdfReadError(exc.__repr__())
                  logger_warning(exc.__repr__(), __name__)
                  retval = DictionaryObject()
                  retval.update(data)
                  return retval  # return partial data
              if not data.get(key):
                  data[key] = value
          return DictionaryObject(data)
  ```

test "rank1627: recursion and limit errors are hard errors"
  lang python
  file pypdf/generic/_data_structures.py
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  reject VYQL-DOS-050
  code
  ```
  class DictionaryObject(dict):
      @staticmethod
      def read_from_stream(stream, pdf, forced_encoding=None):
          tmp = stream.read(2)
          if tmp != b"<<":
              raise PdfReadError(STREAM_TRUNCATED_PREMATURELY)
          data = {}
          while True:
              tok = read_non_whitespace(stream)
              if tok == b"\x00":
                  continue
              if tok == b"%":
                  stream.seek(-1, 1)
                  skip_over_comment(stream)
                  continue
              if not tok:
                  raise PdfStreamError(STREAM_TRUNCATED_PREMATURELY)
              if tok == b">":
                  stream.read(1)
                  break
              stream.seek(-1, 1)
              try:
                  try:
                      key = read_object(stream, pdf)
                      if isinstance(key, NullObject):
                          break
                      if not isinstance(key, NameObject):
                          raise PdfReadError(
                              f"Expecting a NameObject for key but found {key!r}"
                          )
                  except PdfReadError as exc:
                      if pdf is not None and pdf.strict:
                          raise
                      logger_warning(exc.__repr__(), __name__)
                      continue
                  tok = read_non_whitespace(stream)
                  stream.seek(-1, 1)
                  value = read_object(stream, pdf, forced_encoding)
              except (RecursionError, LimitReachedError) as exc:
                  raise PdfReadError(exc.__repr__())
              except Exception as exc:
                  if pdf is not None and pdf.strict:
                      raise PdfReadError(exc.__repr__())
                  logger_warning(exc.__repr__(), __name__)
                  retval = DictionaryObject()
                  retval.update(data)
                  return retval  # return partial data
              if not data.get(key):
                  data[key] = value
          return DictionaryObject(data)
  ```

test "rank1627: the cycle guard raises the class the parser absorbs"
  lang python
  file pypdf/_reader.py
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  reject VYQL-DOS-050
  code
  ```
  class PdfReader(PdfDocCommon):
      def get_object(self, indirect_reference):
          retval = self.cache_get_indirect_object(
              indirect_reference.generation, indirect_reference.idnum
          )
          if retval is not None:
              return retval
          if (
              indirect_reference.generation != 0
              and indirect_reference.generation not in self.xref_entry
          ):
              if self.strict:
                  raise PdfReadError(f"Object {indirect_reference!r} not found.")
          current_object = (indirect_reference.idnum, indirect_reference.generation)
          if current_object in self._known_objects:
              raise PdfReadError(f"Detected loop with self reference for {indirect_reference!r}.")
          self._known_objects.add(current_object)
          retval = read_object(self.stream, self)
          self._known_objects.remove(current_object)
          return retval
  ```

